# Normalise line endings.
#
# Development happens on Windows, deployment is Linux containers. A shell
# script committed with CRLF fails inside the container with
# "bad interpreter: /bin/sh^M", which is an obscure error for an obvious
# cause. Forcing LF on everything that a Linux process executes or parses
# removes the class entirely.

* text=auto eol=lf

*.sh      text eol=lf
*.sql     text eol=lf
*.yml     text eol=lf
*.yaml    text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
Caddyfile text eol=lf
.env.example text eol=lf

# Binary, never touched.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.xlsx binary
